  "description": "<p>LaSalle College Vancouver (LCV) is a private post-secondary institution located in Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada. It was established in 1998 but renamed the Art Institute of Vancouver and was later renamed LaSalle College Vancouver in 2017 after being acquired by the LCI Education Network.</p><p>Around 620 international students are enrolled in courses annually at LaSalle College Vancouver annually. Popular programmes include Fashion Design, Graphic Design, Game Programming, and more.</p><h2>What is the LaSalle College acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The LaSalle College acceptance rate is 64%.</p> <p>LaSalle College provides a modern campus in Vancouver's downtown area, which is easily accessible by public transit. The library is comprehensive as it provides a range of learning resources, from books to journals, in a range of fields. State-of-the-art computer labs provide first-rate technology to students so they can unlock their potential in areas like Game Programming or Interior Design. Students even have access to a fully stocked kitchen so there is convenient access to healthy meals</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The creative buzz reverberating around campus makes students feel a part of a connected community of young people with inspiring ideas. The Student Affairs Department provides students with a range of interesting student clubs and organisations, including French club, Photography club, and Dance club. Guest speaker events and workshops are available throughout the year to keep students academically active and socially engaged in campus life.</p>",
